    /// `[[source: ctlseqs]]` records the errata directly: "testing a DEC VT420[m
    /// in 1996 showed that the documented code for a valid or invalid response[m
    /// to DECRQSS was reversed", and that vttest and DEC STD 070 agree with the[m
    /// tested behaviour rather than with the VT420 and VT525 manuals. baud[m
    /// follows xterm, which is what applications are written against. Getting[m
    /// this backwards would tell every application that every setting it asked[m
    /// about is unsupported.[m
